    "gm_notes": "<p>The standard beast of burden in most human and Jaffa settlements, the draft horse is large, strong, and relatively easy to train. While not violent by nature, a kick or trampling from a horse can easily split a skull. This beast was built by selecting a CR 12 Quadruped (2 hoof attacks) and choosing its abilities to make it big, strong, and hardy.</p><p>Example beast, Core Rulebook pp.314-317.</p>",
